      "a": "wer:\nGlobalisation has affected the role of the state in developing countries in several ways. Traditionally, many states followed a welfare model, providing social services and protecting domestic industries. With globalisation, there has been a shift toward a minimalist state focusing mainly on law, order, and security, while market forces and multinational companies now play a larger role in economic and social sectors. This has reduced the state's capacity in some areas but also enabled it to use advanced technology to regulate and monitor society more effectively. While some argue that this shift enhances efficiency and economic growth, critics worry that it increases inequality and leaves vulnerable groups less protected, pressing the need for social safety nets and institutional safeguards."
